From 3af9c2dd5d254512176ebbb2c5c58003ca413c24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:28:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] editing: insertParagraph in inline content of an editing host
 like Chrome

Enter in the middle of "ab" directly in a <div contenteditable> gave
a<div><br></div>b, where Chrome gives a<div>b</div>: the line of inline content
in the editing host has no paragraph of its own, and step 11 of the spec wraps
it before splitting, which Chrome does not do.

When the position is in inline content directly in the editing host,
insertParagraph now does what Chrome does: at the end of the content an empty
paragraph follows (keeping the inline elements the caret is in), at the start
of a line that begins the host or follows a block an empty paragraph precedes
the line, and otherwise the inline elements around the position are split and
everything after it moves into a new paragraph, with a <br> keeping a line
that would otherwise collapse and a trailing space turned into a no-break
space. The paragraph element follows defaultParagraphSeparator.

Like Chrome, a collapsed selection is not deleted first, which canonicalized
the white space before the caret ("ab |" became "ab&nbsp;").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../execcommand/commands/insertparagraph.rs   | 253 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 246 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/script/dom/execcommand/commands/insertparagraph.rs b/components/script/dom/execcommand/commands/insertparagraph.rs
index 17559a339b2..e1da3e73a85 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/execcommand/commands/insertparagraph.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/execcommand/commands/insertparagraph.rs
@@ -2,16 +2,21 @@
